# Environment Variables Configuration

This file contains sample environment variables for the MCP System. Copy this file to `.env` in the backend directory and update with your actual values.

```
# Server Configuration
PORT=5000
NODE_ENV=development

# MongoDB Configuration
MONGODB_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/mcp-system

# JWT Configuration
JWT_SECRET=your-secure-jwt-secret-key-replace-this

# OAuth Configuration
OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=your-oauth-client-id
OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=your-oauth-client-secret
OAUTH_CALLBACK_URL=http://localhost:5000/api/auth/callback

# Frontend URL
FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:3000

# LLM API Keys
# Note: Never commit actual API keys to version control
# These are placeholders - replace with your actual keys in the .env file
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your-anthropic-api-key
OPENAI_API_KEY=your-openai-api-key
OPENAI_ORG_ID=your-openai-org-id

# GitHub Configuration
GITHUB_TOKEN=your-github-token
```

## Security Notes

1. Keep your `.env` file secure and never commit it to version control
2. Use different API keys for development and production
3. Rotate API keys regularly
4. Consider using a secrets management service in production
5. Set appropriate permissions for the `.env` file (e.g., `chmod 600 .env`)
